  "question": {
    "text": "The electric field between the two parallel plates of a capacitor of $1.5 \\mu \\mathrm{F}$ capacitance drops to one third of its initial value in $6.6 \\mu \\mathrm{s}$ when the plates are connected by a thin wire.\nThe resistance of this wire is _____$\\Omega$. (Given, $\\log 3=1.1$ )",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "4",
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{aligned} & \\mathrm{E}=\\frac{\\mathrm{E}_0}{3} \\Rightarrow \\mathrm{V}=\\frac{\\mathrm{V}_0}{3} \\\\ & \\frac{\\mathrm{V}_0}{3}=\\mathrm{V}_0 \\mathrm{e}^{-\\frac{\\mathrm{t}}{\\tau}} \\\\ & \\mathrm{t}=\\tau \\ell \\mathrm{n} 3 \\\\ & 6.6 \\times 10^{-6}=\\mathrm{R}\\left(1.5 \\times 10^{-6}\\right)(1.1) \\\\ & \\mathrm{R}=\\frac{6}{1.5}=4 \\Omega\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
